minimal shadowing covers (any size) by ratios in (0,1) with denominator dividing c
a cover is MINIMAL when no proper subset shadows

c= 4: no shadowing cover of size <= 6

c= 5: no shadowing cover of size <= 6

c= 6: no shadowing cover of size <= 6

c= 7: no shadowing cover of size <= 6

c= 8: minimal covers have size 5; count 1
        ['1/8', '3/8', '1/2', '5/8', '7/8']

c= 9: minimal covers have size 6; count 2
        ['1/9', '2/9', '1/3', '5/9', '7/9', '8/9']
        ['1/9', '2/9', '5/9', '2/3', '7/9', '8/9']

c=10: minimal covers have size 5; count 4
        ['1/10', '1/5', '3/10', '1/2', '7/10']
        ['1/10', '3/10', '2/5', '1/2', '7/10']
        ['1/10', '3/10', '1/2', '3/5', '7/10']
        ['1/10', '3/10', '1/2', '7/10', '4/5']

c=11: minimal covers have size 6; count 2
        ['1/11', '2/11', '5/11', '6/11', '7/11', '8/11']
        ['1/11', '2/11', '6/11', '7/11', '8/11', '10/11']

